# DeFi Protocol Rules — Aquarius DeFi Lab

## Abstraction First
- Each protocol must be implemented via an adapter.
- No protocol logic should leak into UI or shared core logic.

## Consistency
- Normalize protocol data into common internal models.
- Use shared terminology across protocols.

## Extensibility
- Adding a new protocol should not require refactoring existing ones.
- Favor plug-in style architectures.

## Safety
- Protocol data can be incomplete, delayed, or adversarial.
- Never assume correctness without validation.

## Purpose Alignment
- Protocol features must serve the core promise:
  Making earning opportunities and risks visible.

